From bfae23bdd2f7d25d37a3ffbac2abb22dd27f44de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:32:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 304/333] CLI: --export-drawings writes the drawing pages as
 PDF without the screen

A PDF of a TechDraw page needed the GUI (TechDrawGui.exportPageAsPdf): the
engine field test started the GUI for each drawing, 2 minutes a sheet.
FreeCADCmd model.FCStd --export-drawings out.pdf (and
DrawingPdf.export(path, out, pages=None)) runs a child FreeCADCmd that starts
the GUI offscreen, opens the file without a 3D view (offscreen has no
OpenGL; opening with one hung), waits for the views' lines and writes one
PDF a page (out.pdf, or out_<page>.pdf for more pages, or a name with
{page}). The child ends without tearing the GUI down, which crashed in
FreeCADCmd. The main window is not hidden: hidden, the lines came out
thick. 10 s for the connecting rod's drawing; no page: exit code 1.

Test: FreeCADCmd -t TestDrawingPdf

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
